 {"question":"Which layer–cell-shape pairing is correct in stratified columnar epithelium?","choices":["Superficial: polyhedral; basal: columnar.","Superficial: columnar; middle: polyhedral.","Middle: columnar; basal: polyhedral.","Superficial: cuboidal; middle: flat squamous."],"answer_index":1},
 {"question":"A tissue has columnar superficial cells and deeper polyhedral cells that are usually smaller. Which location agrees with this description?","choices":["Kidney tubule lining.","Blood-vessel lining.","Sweat-gland duct lining.","Urethral lining."],"answer_index":3},
 {"question":"Which statement about stratified columnar epithelium is incorrect?","choices":["Its superficial cells are polyhedral and usually smaller.","Its middle cells are polyhedral and usually smaller.","Its basal cells are polyhedral and usually smaller.","Its superficial cells are columnar."],"answer_index":0},
 {"question":"Which comparison of superficial cells in stratified cuboidal and stratified columnar epithelia is correct?","choices":["Cuboidal: columnar; columnar: cuboidal.","Cuboidal: flat; columnar: columnar.","Cuboidal: cuboidal; columnar: columnar.","Cuboidal: cuboidal; columnar: polyhedral."],"answer_index":2},
 {"question":"Which tissue–location pairing is correct?","choices":["Simple columnar — urethral lining.","Stratified columnar — urethral lining.","Pseudostratified columnar — intestinal lining.","Stratified columnar — tracheal lining."],"answer_index":1},
 {"question":"Which complete set of features applies to stratified columnar epithelium?","choices":["Cuboidal superficial cells, deeper polyhedral cells, urethral lining, protection.","Columnar superficial cells, deeper polyhedral cells, tracheal lining, protection and secretion.","Columnar superficial cells, deeper flat squamous cells, urethral lining, protection.","Columnar superficial cells, deeper polyhedral and usually smaller cells, urethral lining, protection."],"answer_index":3}
