 {"question":"Which group lists locations of transitional epithelium?","choices":["Urinary bladder, urethra, and kidney tubules.","Urinary bladder, ureter, and seminiferous tubules.","Urinary bladder, ureter, and renal pelvis.","Urethra, ureter, and sweat-gland ducts."],"answer_index":2},
 {"question":"How does transitional epithelium perform protection?","choices":["It allows organs to expand and contract without cell damage or tearing.","It allows organs to expand and contract using cilia.","It performs diffusion and filtration in the organs it lines.","It performs secretion and absorption in the organs it lines."],"answer_index":0},
 {"question":"Which sequence describes transitional epithelial cell shapes from superficial to middle to basal layers?","choices":["Umbrella-shaped → cuboidal → polyhedral.","Polyhedral → umbrella-shaped → cuboidal.","Cuboidal → polyhedral → umbrella-shaped.","Umbrella-shaped → polyhedral → cuboidal."],"answer_index":3},
 {"question":"Which statement about transitional epithelium is incorrect?","choices":["Its superficial cells are large and umbrella-shaped.","Its middle cells are cuboidal and rest on the basement membrane.","Its superficial cells have one or two nuclei.","It lines the urinary bladder, ureter, and renal pelvis."],"answer_index":1},
 {"question":"Which complete set of features applies to transitional epithelium?","choices":["Umbrella-shaped superficial, cuboidal middle, polyhedral basal cells; protection.","Columnar superficial, polyhedral middle, cuboidal basal cells; urinary bladder lining.","Umbrella-shaped superficial, polyhedral middle, cuboidal basal cells; permits expansion and contraction without cell damage.","Umbrella-shaped superficial, polyhedral middle, cuboidal basal cells; diffusion and filtration."],"answer_index":2}
